<article class="crs-lesson">
    <h3><span class="crs-lesson-num">Lesson 1.1</span> The Agent's Role &amp; The Complete Sales Cycle</h3>

    <span class="crs-sub-label">1.1.1 More Than Just Showing Units</span>
    <p>Picture a real estate agent, and you probably imagine someone driving buyers from unit to unit and unlocking doors. That's part of the job — but only a small part. A real transaction usually stretches over weeks, sometimes months, and touches financing, legal paperwork, inspections, and a lot of nervous decision-making on the client's side. Someone has to hold all of that together and keep it moving. That someone is you.</p>
    <p>Because so much of the work happens off-camera — a follow-up call to a lender, a clarifying text to a title officer, a gentle nudge to a hesitant buyer — clients rarely see the full scope of what you do until something goes wrong and you're the one who fixes it. Understanding this upfront changes how you plan your time: showings are the visible 10% of the job, and the other 90% is what actually gets deals to the finish line.</p>

    <span class="crs-sub-label">1.1.2 The Three Roles You Play</span>
    <p>Tap each role below to see what it actually looks like day to day.</p>
